# Cell-level gate: a simulation of admission rules and a replay on the Ticket 009b pool

This page belongs to the cell-gate study in the [README](../README.md#cell-level-gate-confirmatory-study). Everything on it is exploratory: the simulation tests whether the existing admission rules can control a margin-level loss in one cell at a budget the project can run, and the replay applies the same rules to the Ticket 009b candidates. Neither changes a committed result, label or verdict of the cell-gate study.

## Setup (Exploratory)

- **Frozen plan.** `plans/ticket-013-sim-plan.json` (sha256 {{t013.settings.plan_sha256}}) and its addendum `plans/ticket-013-sim-plan-addendum.json` (sha256 {{t013.settings.addendum_sha256}}) were frozen and tagged before any simulation code ran. Results: `results/ticket-013/sim.json` (sha256 {{hash.t013_sim}}), `sim-gain-correction.json` (sha256 {{hash.t013_gain}}), `replay-009b.json` (sha256 {{hash.t013_replay}}) and `replay-009b-c6.json` (sha256 {{hash.t013_replay_c6}}).
- **No LLM calls.** Each simulated pool holds {{t013.settings.candidates}} candidates; every condition uses {{t013.settings.pools}} pools and {{t013.settings.n_boot}} bootstrap draws. Before the main run, the code reproduced the null label rates of the Ticket 009b planning simulation (Local Harm {{t013.gate.local_harm.rate}} against {{t013.gate.local_harm.registered}}, Severe {{t013.gate.severe.rate}} against {{t013.gate.severe.registered}}).
- **Baselines.** Baseline a uses S0's case rates from its calibration records (the ceiling and floor cells of Ticket 009b kept as a stress test). Baseline b uses S0′'s case rates from ten Dev-A cases per cell; it is a stylized mid-range structure, not an estimate of S0′.
- **Gates.** C4 and C5 as in the cell-gate study; C6-IUT = C4 and, in every cell, a one-sided lower bound of δ_c above −m_c (Tango score as the primary bound, the exact conditional bound as the secondary, α = {{t013.param.alpha}}); SAGE λ1 and λ2, a per-cell SAGE cap, and a credit-type gate (ε = {{t013.param.credit_eps}}). **SAGE, the per-cell cap and the credit-type gate are our own one-round implementations of rules from other papers, and τ = {{t013.param.sage_tau}} is our value; the SAGE paper tuned its parameters on held-out data.**
- **Go rule (frozen).** In baseline a or b, a combination (gate, n_c, m_c) counts toward Go when the worst false accept over the inadmissible scenarios and both loss-cell placements is at most {{t013.threshold.false_accept}}, the acceptance of a representative Useful candidate is at least {{t013.threshold.useful_power}}, and Dev-B needs at most {{t013.threshold.episodes}} episodes; a combination within {{t013.threshold.borderline_se}} MC SE of a threshold is borderline and does not count.

