## What these results support (Exploratory)

- **Large local losses (the Severe candidates of Ticket 009b).** Of the {{t013.replay.all.labels.severe}} Severe candidates in the Ticket 009b pool, C4 accepted {{t013.replay.all.C4.severe}}, C5 {{t013.replay.all.C5.severe}}, SAGE λ1 {{t013.replay.all.SAGE_l1.severe}} and SAGE λ2 {{t013.replay.all.SAGE_l2.severe}}. C5 and SAGE (our implementation) both filtered most of the Severe candidates that C4 accepted. This gives no evidence that C5 is better than SAGE.
- **Margin-level local losses (simulation, one cell at −m_c).** At m_c = {{t013.margin.m05}}, C4, SAGE and C5 did not control false acceptance at any n_c (baseline a, n_c {{t013.nc.150}}: C4 {{t013.dec.a.C4.n150.m05.false_accept}}, SAGE λ1 {{t013.dec.a.SAGE_l1.n150.m05.false_accept}}, C5 {{t013.dec.a.C5.n150.m05.false_accept}}), and only C6-IUT controlled it at the α level ({{t013.dec.a.C6_IUT.n150.m05.false_accept}}). C5 is a filter for large losses; it does not control losses of the size of the margin. The cost of C6-IUT is the sample per cell: in baseline a it met the Go rule only from n_c {{t013.nc.150}}. At m_c = {{t013.margin.m10}} and n_c {{t013.nc.300}}, C5 also met the Go rule in baseline a ({{t013.dec.a.C5.n300.m10.false_accept}}).
- **Per-cell SAGE and the credit-type gate rejected practically everything,** in the simulation (largest representative Useful power: per-cell SAGE {{t013.dec.b.SAGE_cell_l1.n70.m05.useful_power}}, credit-type {{t013.dec.a.credit.n70.m05.useful_power}}) and in the replay ({{t013.replay.all.SAGE_cell_l1.accepted}} and {{t013.replay.all.credit.accepted}} accepted).
- **C6-IUT on the Ticket 009b pool.** At {{t013.nc.70}} per cell, C6-IUT (Tango, m_c {{t013.margin.m05}}) was very conservative ({{t013.c6.all.tango_m05.accepted}} accepted, {{t013.c6.all.tango_m05.clean_useful}} of {{t013.replay.all.labels.clean_useful}} Clean Useful). This agrees with the simulated power at n_c {{t013.nc.70}} ({{t013.dec.a.C6_IUT.n70.m05.useful_power}} in baseline a). The exact conditional bound accepted more ({{t013.c6.all.exact_m05.accepted}}) and admitted {{t013.c6.all.exact_m05.severe}} Severe candidate, which agrees with its coverage shortfall in the simulation.

## Limits of this simulation (Exploratory)

- **Our implementations.** SAGE, the per-cell SAGE cap and the credit-type gate are simplified one-round versions; τ = {{t013.param.sage_tau}} is our value. Their papers' results are not reproduced here.
- **Exact conditional coverage below nominal.** The one-sided bounds should cover the true cell effect with probability {{t013.param.nominal_coverage}}. Over all baselines, n_c, m_c and scenarios, the exact conditional bound covered it in {{t013.cov.all.exact.min}} to {{t013.cov.all.exact.max}} of the cells, and the Tango bound in {{t013.cov.all.tango.min}} to {{t013.cov.all.tango.max}}.
- **The percentile bootstrap demonstration gave no information.** In its one condition (baseline a, no effect in any cell, n_c {{t013.nc.70}}, m_c {{t013.margin.m05}}), C6-IUT accepted {{t013.demo.percentile}} of candidates with the percentile bound, {{t013.demo.tango}} with Tango and {{t013.demo.exact}} with the exact conditional bound, and C4 alone {{t013.demo.C4}}; the condition does not separate the bounds.
- **The realized L1–L2 coupling was small.** The copula correlation was {{t013.param.coupling_rho}}, but the binary (phi) correlation it produced in the simulated calibration runs was {{t013.phi.coupled.traffic_spike.min}} to {{t013.phi.coupled.traffic_spike.max}} in traffic_spike and {{t013.phi.coupled.dependency_failure.min}} to {{t013.phi.coupled.dependency_failure.max}} in dependency_failure (bad_deployment: undefined, L1 succeeds in every case). The coupled rows below hold under this small correlation. For description only, the Ticket 009b calibration records give {{t013.phi.009b.traffic_spike}} (traffic_spike) and {{t013.phi.009b.dependency_failure}} (dependency_failure).
- **Oracle label uncertainty at {{t013.param.oracle_per_cell}} incidents per cell.** The share of candidates whose simulated oracle interval crossed ±ε was, at n_c {{t013.nc.70}} and m_c {{t013.margin.m05}}: baseline a, {{t013.orc.a.null}} (no effect), {{t013.orc.a.useful}} (representative Useful), {{t013.orc.a.empirical}} (empirical); baseline b, {{t013.orc.b.null}}, {{t013.orc.b.useful}} and {{t013.orc.b.empirical}}.
- **Gain values come only from the correction file.** The gain per proposal in `results/ticket-013/sim.json` is invalid: the pool sums were truncated to integers before the MC SE. The values below are read from `results/ticket-013/sim-gain-correction.json`, which recomputes them from the same checkpoints; gain is not part of the Go rule.

